WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.687 --> 00:00:02.901
- I have succeeded because I had to.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.922
Well, I have made a lot of great products,

00:00:04.922 --> 00:00:07.458
but there's also been some real duds.

00:00:07.458 --> 00:00:10.156
That's what successful
business is all about,

00:00:10.156 --> 00:00:13.496
spotting new opportunities
and exploiting them.

00:00:13.496 --> 00:00:17.998
I have to be half-dead
not to not go to work.

00:00:17.998 --> 00:00:21.717
I got a philosophy, which
is stick to what you know.

00:00:21.717 --> 00:00:25.228
Generally, people that stay with you

00:00:25.228 --> 00:00:28.000
are motivated not
necessarily just by money,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.248
but they're motivated by the enjoyment.

00:00:30.248 --> 00:00:31.926
Answer emails immediately,

00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:33.911
answer people's questions immediately.

00:00:33.911 --> 00:00:35.266
That's been my success.

00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:37.194
I would not take on something

00:00:37.194 --> 00:00:40.037
that I couldn't see a light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:00:40.037 --> 00:00:42.506
Because if you engross yourself too much

00:00:42.506 --> 00:00:44.598
in the day to day running of the business,

00:00:44.598 --> 00:00:47.556
you might find that the
world is passing you by.

00:00:47.556 --> 00:00:49.218
I can only talk from my experience.

00:00:49.218 --> 00:00:51.216
My products did the talking.

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:54.247
- He's an English business
magnate, political advisor,

00:00:54.247 --> 00:00:55.867
and television personality.

00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:58.020
In 2007, he sold his remaining interest

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.831
in his Amstrad company, which
was his most well-known,

00:01:00.831 --> 00:01:02.732
and most successful business venture.

00:01:02.732 --> 00:01:06.435
He has an estimate fortune
of 1.4 billion pounds.

00:01:06.435 --> 00:01:07.970
He's Alan Michael Sugar,

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.462
and here are his Top 10 Rules for Success.

00:01:10.462 --> 00:01:11.672
(whooshing)

00:01:11.672 --> 00:01:13.720
(booming)

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.887
- I don't wish to alienate people here

00:01:18.682 --> 00:01:20.806
with about what I'm about to say.

00:01:20.806 --> 00:01:24.473
But you know, your
destiny is in your hands.

00:01:28.473 --> 00:01:31.992
I have succeeded because I had to.

00:01:31.992 --> 00:01:34.825
No one sorted anything out for me.

00:01:36.681 --> 00:01:39.541
I didn't ask, go to any
government and said,

00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:42.112
pretty please, find me some work,

00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:44.713
please, and do something for me,

00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:47.800
because it was a waste of bloody time.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.224
Simply that, a waste of time.

00:01:50.224 --> 00:01:53.571
And if I was going to do
something, I had to do it myself.

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:57.560
And that's it, and I would
say to every one of you here,

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.378
don't sit around relying upon, magically,

00:02:01.378 --> 00:02:03.748
some government going
to create an environment

00:02:03.748 --> 00:02:05.595
that's going to make it easy for you

00:02:05.595 --> 00:02:07.149
to find work and find jobs.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:10.134
You've got to go out there
and fight for it yourself.

00:02:10.134 --> 00:02:12.771
I'm sorry to say, I
can't give you any other,

00:02:12.771 --> 00:02:14.854
any other form of advice.

00:02:16.192 --> 00:02:18.471
If you want something
bad enough, you do it.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.257
And if you look at some of these wannabes

00:02:21.257 --> 00:02:23.141
have made themselves television stars

00:02:23.141 --> 00:02:26.558
and pop stars and all that type of stuff,

00:02:27.611 --> 00:02:30.488
they have a desire to want to be famous,

00:02:30.488 --> 00:02:34.187
and they don't stop until
they're recognized and they do.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:37.462
And half the people that you
see on television these days

00:02:37.462 --> 00:02:39.367
in the entertainments industry are those

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:42.350
that had the determination
that wanted to do it.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.914
And I'll add a little rider to that,

00:02:43.914 --> 00:02:45.731
none of them could bloody sing.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:48.731
(audience laughing)

00:02:50.181 --> 00:02:51.511
Not helpful, right, I mean,

00:02:51.511 --> 00:02:53.083
you didn't find that helpful answer.

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:56.437
But you're going to control
your destiny, I'm telling you.

00:02:56.437 --> 00:02:58.004
No one else is going to do it.

00:02:58.004 --> 00:02:59.747
Not unless you got a rich dad.

00:02:59.747 --> 00:03:00.941
(audience laughing)

00:03:00.941 --> 00:03:03.177
Have you got a rich dad, a rich uncle?

00:03:03.177 --> 00:03:04.285
No, well then, that's it.

00:03:04.285 --> 00:03:06.268
You're going to have to do it yourself.

00:03:06.268 --> 00:03:10.435
And then you have to be realistic
also, and not a dreamer.

00:03:11.517 --> 00:03:15.049
And that's one thing people
said about me after the event.

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:17.733
I talk as if I've always
made great products.

00:03:17.733 --> 00:03:19.712
Well, I have made a lot of great products,

00:03:19.712 --> 00:03:22.827
but there's also been some real duds.

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:24.566
And one of the things about me is,

00:03:24.566 --> 00:03:28.275
is that as much as I, as well
as I know the marketplace,

00:03:28.275 --> 00:03:30.734
and know if I got a hit on my hand,

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:33.501
I also know when I've got a dud on my hand

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.749
and know to cut, wipe your face, get out,

00:03:35.749 --> 00:03:37.792
and clear it out and get rid of it,

00:03:37.792 --> 00:03:40.321
don't waste any more time, move on.

00:03:40.321 --> 00:03:44.071
And I think a lot of
people are not prepared

00:03:45.452 --> 00:03:48.308
to recognize that
something's been a failure.

00:03:48.308 --> 00:03:52.717
And you're successful
by, on many occasions,

00:03:52.717 --> 00:03:56.503
by learning mistakes,
from your failures also.

00:03:56.503 --> 00:03:58.952
A successful business person needs to

00:03:58.952 --> 00:04:02.224
exploit the market or the
sector that they are in.

00:04:02.224 --> 00:04:04.687
They need to have a great
understanding of it.

00:04:04.687 --> 00:04:07.625
They need to constantly
monitor the marketplace

00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:09.471
and spot opportunities.

00:04:09.471 --> 00:04:12.087
That's what successful
business is all about,

00:04:12.087 --> 00:04:15.858
spotting new opportunities
and exploiting them.

00:04:15.858 --> 00:04:19.173
Most success stories in
expansion of businesses

00:04:19.173 --> 00:04:21.423
are based upon enhancements

00:04:22.327 --> 00:04:26.492
learnt from the core business
that you're already in.

00:04:26.492 --> 00:04:29.232
Adding additional features to products,

00:04:29.232 --> 00:04:31.311
expanding product ranges,

00:04:31.311 --> 00:04:34.968
ideas that come from what
you're already doing,

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:36.723
particularly in manufacturing.

00:04:36.723 --> 00:04:39.520
Your own employees could actually come up

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.360
with some spark of genius

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.693
in streamlining the production process,

00:04:43.693 --> 00:04:46.248
something that you may have
never thought about before,

00:04:46.248 --> 00:04:48.983
something that could save
you lots and lots of money.

00:04:48.983 --> 00:04:52.017
Or suddenly come up
with an idea based upon

00:04:52.017 --> 00:04:55.070
the product that you're
producing that is allied to it.

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.244
When you come from

00:04:56.244 --> 00:04:59.366
the working class
background that I come from,

00:04:59.366 --> 00:05:00.449
I feel guilty

00:05:05.463 --> 00:05:09.629
at 10 to five, if I'm not in the office.

00:05:09.629 --> 00:05:11.865
I know that might sound strange to you,

00:05:11.865 --> 00:05:13.948
but there's a work ethic

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.980
that I have to be half-dead

00:05:19.738 --> 00:05:21.555
not to not go to work.

00:05:21.555 --> 00:05:25.722
It's kind of a work ethic
that's built into me, you know?

00:05:27.205 --> 00:05:30.455
But nevertheless, having said all that,

00:05:31.624 --> 00:05:34.418
the weekends, that was it, it's over,

00:05:34.418 --> 00:05:36.532
switch off like a light Friday night

00:05:36.532 --> 00:05:38.373
as you got back from the
office or from the work

00:05:38.373 --> 00:05:40.143
or from the factory, whatever.

00:05:40.143 --> 00:05:43.130
No matter what was
buzzing around in my head,

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.238
it was off like a light
switch, and that's it.

00:05:46.238 --> 00:05:47.629
Don't let it interfere,

00:05:47.629 --> 00:05:50.173
very rarely let it
interfere with the weekend.

00:05:50.173 --> 00:05:53.424
And then Monday morning,
bang, back on it again,

00:05:53.424 --> 00:05:55.507
as if you flicked the switch on again.

00:05:55.507 --> 00:05:59.435
So I think was a bit of
discipline in that respect.

00:05:59.435 --> 00:06:03.602
I got a philosophy, which
is stick to what you know.

00:06:04.848 --> 00:06:08.973
And real estate, as I
explained in detail already,

00:06:08.973 --> 00:06:11.306
is something that I know now

00:06:12.724 --> 00:06:15.776
and of course, electronics
is something that I know,

00:06:15.776 --> 00:06:18.526
and the answer, very simply, is no,

00:06:18.526 --> 00:06:22.689
I wouldn't invest in a business
that I didn't understand.

00:06:22.689 --> 00:06:25.239
I would invest in
businesses that I understood

00:06:25.239 --> 00:06:28.572
but didn't necessarily want to run them.

00:06:30.758 --> 00:06:32.612
And I think that's a good philosophy also,

00:06:32.612 --> 00:06:34.220
is to stick to what you know.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.558
But generally, people that stay with you

00:06:37.558 --> 00:06:40.406
are motivated not
necessarily just by money,

00:06:40.406 --> 00:06:43.042
but they're motivated by the enjoyment

00:06:43.042 --> 00:06:45.668
or the excitement of what you're creating

00:06:45.668 --> 00:06:49.299
and the fact that you
make them part of a team.

00:06:49.299 --> 00:06:50.773
And that they can see that

00:06:50.773 --> 00:06:52.565
they're actually achieving something

00:06:52.565 --> 00:06:55.052
towards the goal of the organization.

00:06:55.052 --> 00:06:57.295
And I think if you ostracize people

00:06:57.295 --> 00:07:00.201
or you don't show them your
appreciation in that way,

00:07:00.201 --> 00:07:03.852
then you can expect them
not to show that loyalty.

00:07:03.852 --> 00:07:05.902
- When you've gone from
looking out of windows

00:07:05.902 --> 00:07:06.990
at classrooms,

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.131
to having a very regimented
timetable on the weekends,

00:07:09.131 --> 00:07:13.375
how did you develop such
a good self-discipline?

00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:15.391
- I don't know, I am very disciplined.

00:07:15.391 --> 00:07:18.763
That's all I could say to
you, very, very, disciplined,

00:07:18.763 --> 00:07:20.430
a creature of habit.

00:07:22.847 --> 00:07:26.073
What's that thing, is it called
OCD, or something like that.

00:07:26.073 --> 00:07:29.419
If you look at my desk, you'll
see all the pens lined up,

00:07:29.419 --> 00:07:31.913
like that, and the piece
of paper over here,

00:07:31.913 --> 00:07:33.606
and a cup over there and all that.

00:07:33.606 --> 00:07:36.659
I'm just very disciplined, that's it.

00:07:36.659 --> 00:07:39.265
I think in business and in life,

00:07:39.265 --> 00:07:42.848
I work on the principle
of clearing my desk

00:07:44.986 --> 00:07:47.236
every minute, or every day.

00:07:49.617 --> 00:07:52.527
So answer emails immediately,

00:07:52.527 --> 00:07:54.480
answer people's questions immediately.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.185
That's been my success
in running my company,

00:07:58.185 --> 00:08:02.264
that I'm there to, like a
springboard, if you like,

00:08:02.264 --> 00:08:06.191
for employees to tell
me what their issue is

00:08:06.191 --> 00:08:09.988
and then to give them a quick resolution

00:08:09.988 --> 00:08:12.209
to it so they can get on and deal with it.

00:08:12.209 --> 00:08:14.209
So that's my discipline.

00:08:16.678 --> 00:08:19.888
I would heartily recommend
it to all of you.

00:08:19.888 --> 00:08:23.626
If you decide to become,
you should be disciplined,

00:08:23.626 --> 00:08:26.173
you should discipline yourself.

00:08:26.173 --> 00:08:28.676
Because it's not a bad way of life.

00:08:28.676 --> 00:08:32.759
We've been through an era
of massive bankruptcies

00:08:33.765 --> 00:08:36.571
or liquidations and receiverships,

00:08:36.571 --> 00:08:38.253
particularly in the property world

00:08:38.253 --> 00:08:42.079
where lots of money has
been lent against assets

00:08:42.079 --> 00:08:44.917
which were over-valued, for example.

00:08:44.917 --> 00:08:48.500
I, fortunately, didn't
play in that market.

00:08:50.309 --> 00:08:52.552
My son's in this business with me,

00:08:52.552 --> 00:08:55.372
and we kind of sat around
watching what was going on,

00:08:55.372 --> 00:08:58.789
and knowing that this is a forced-market.

00:08:59.813 --> 00:09:03.255
I would not take on something
that I couldn't pay for,

00:09:03.255 --> 00:09:06.218
myself, I would not take on something

00:09:06.218 --> 00:09:09.761
that I couldn't see a light
at the end of the tunnel,

00:09:09.761 --> 00:09:12.563
where we come out of it.

00:09:12.563 --> 00:09:15.770
And I know that's pretty
much stating the obvious,

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:18.052
and it doesn't apply to all businesses,

00:09:18.052 --> 00:09:19.959
but I think it's a good philosophy.

00:09:19.959 --> 00:09:22.636
That's to always have a
kind of a wake up call,

00:09:22.636 --> 00:09:26.342
whether it be weekly,
monthly, or six-monthly,

00:09:26.342 --> 00:09:30.241
where you are, where you're
going, what you're doing.

00:09:30.241 --> 00:09:31.963
And it's easier in some businesses,

00:09:31.963 --> 00:09:33.976
because you know, it's blatantly obvious

00:09:33.976 --> 00:09:35.670
where you're going in some businesses,

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.349
because if it's a retail business,

00:09:37.349 --> 00:09:39.931
it's, have you got customers
coming across the table

00:09:39.931 --> 00:09:41.533
or the counter for naught?

00:09:41.533 --> 00:09:44.558
In other businesses, particularly
like service businesses,

00:09:44.558 --> 00:09:47.457
where there is no product
that you touch and feel,

00:09:47.457 --> 00:09:51.624
and that your income comes from
being an agent, for example,

00:09:53.537 --> 00:09:55.019
you have to constantly

00:09:55.019 --> 00:09:58.168
look at your overheads and your costs.

00:09:58.168 --> 00:10:01.164
And I think that it is cost-control,

00:10:01.164 --> 00:10:03.577
regular wake up calls,

00:10:03.577 --> 00:10:06.136
regular checks of where you are,

00:10:06.136 --> 00:10:09.780
status checks of where you
are, will keep you afloat.

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:13.612
You need to set aside a day per week,

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:15.610
where you divorce yourself from

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:18.968
the day to day activity of your company.

00:10:18.968 --> 00:10:22.667
You must have someone inside
the company who you trust.

00:10:22.667 --> 00:10:25.757
God forbid, you ever got run
over by a Number Six bus,

00:10:25.757 --> 00:10:28.908
think of that person who
would have to take control

00:10:28.908 --> 00:10:31.547
and put that person in
control for that day,

00:10:31.547 --> 00:10:33.249
or for those two days.

00:10:33.249 --> 00:10:37.074
And then use those two days
to go out into the marketplace

00:10:37.074 --> 00:10:39.514
to find yourself some new business

00:10:39.514 --> 00:10:43.111
or at least observe what your
competitors are getting up to

00:10:43.111 --> 00:10:44.619
and what they're doing

00:10:44.619 --> 00:10:46.574
in order to see how
the market is changing.

00:10:46.574 --> 00:10:49.104
Because if you engross yourself too much

00:10:49.104 --> 00:10:51.214
in the day to day running of the business,

00:10:51.214 --> 00:10:54.200
you might find that the
world is passing you by

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.276
and you're missing opportunities.

00:10:56.276 --> 00:10:57.734
Well, I think that you could be,

00:10:57.734 --> 00:11:00.817
I mean, the point is, is that there's

00:11:02.903 --> 00:11:05.070
the integrity and honesty,

00:11:06.661 --> 00:11:09.052
as far as I'm concerned
goes without saying,

00:11:09.052 --> 00:11:11.529
and you can push that to
one side at the moment.

00:11:11.529 --> 00:11:14.696
Because you can be honest
and have a high integrity,

00:11:14.696 --> 00:11:17.674
but if you've got lousy product,

00:11:17.674 --> 00:11:20.390
or prices are too high, it's irrelevant.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:24.834
So it's a mixture of
spotting opportunities,

00:11:24.834 --> 00:11:27.618
I mean, target from the
top of your own business,

00:11:27.618 --> 00:11:31.073
spotting opportunities,
products, services,

00:11:31.073 --> 00:11:34.573
that you want to offer that do bring value

00:11:35.505 --> 00:11:37.600
to whomever you're going to sell them to,

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.059
and then having the nous
to go and sell them.

00:11:42.059 --> 00:11:45.215
I mean, again, this young
man's question over there,

00:11:45.215 --> 00:11:47.215
it's very, very similar.

00:11:48.628 --> 00:11:52.216
I get asked a lot a similar
question in universities

00:11:52.216 --> 00:11:53.506
and places like this.

00:11:53.506 --> 00:11:56.340
You don't just jump out
of bed one Monday morning

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:59.456
and I want to be Richard Branson,
I'm going to start an airline.

00:11:59.456 --> 00:12:03.064
Like that, I want to start
an airline tomorrow morning.

00:12:03.064 --> 00:12:06.271
Total nonsense, have you got any money?

00:12:06.271 --> 00:12:09.302
No, but I want to start an
airline tomorrow morning.

00:12:09.302 --> 00:12:11.524
And so there's a certain realism

00:12:11.524 --> 00:12:14.274
as to what one month needs to do.

00:12:15.332 --> 00:12:17.700
Secondly, you've got to look at,

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:21.515
you got to also have a
realistic point of view.

00:12:21.515 --> 00:12:25.195
I'm new, I'm starting,
I've got a new business.

00:12:25.195 --> 00:12:27.258
What do I offer somebody?

00:12:27.258 --> 00:12:29.608
What do I offer my potential customer?

00:12:29.608 --> 00:12:31.901
What have I got that
they can't already get

00:12:31.901 --> 00:12:35.114
from 20 or 30 or 40 or 50 other people?

00:12:35.114 --> 00:12:37.993
Because if I'm not offering
anything different,

00:12:37.993 --> 00:12:41.822
then I've got a tough job ahead of me.

00:12:41.822 --> 00:12:44.242
And I think you have to continually

00:12:44.242 --> 00:12:46.569
test yourself on that basis.

00:12:46.569 --> 00:12:49.566
I used to test myself with products.

00:12:49.566 --> 00:12:51.788
Is this a good product or not?

00:12:51.788 --> 00:12:53.588
Well, has anybody else got one?

00:12:53.588 --> 00:12:55.701
Or is it the same as what
other people have got

00:12:55.701 --> 00:12:57.858
but half the price, does it do more,

00:12:57.858 --> 00:13:01.079
has it got different features
on it, is it look better,

00:13:01.079 --> 00:13:02.653
is the market ready for it?

00:13:02.653 --> 00:13:06.153
That's the test and from my point of view,

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.287
I can only talk from my experience,

00:13:10.287 --> 00:13:12.486
my products did the talking.

00:13:12.486 --> 00:13:15.068
You know, I could be the
greatest salesman in the world,

00:13:15.068 --> 00:13:17.306
the most charming person in the world,

00:13:17.306 --> 00:13:18.900
whatever you want to be,

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.696
and you could advertise
and do whatever you want.

00:13:21.696 --> 00:13:25.613
If the product sucks,
then you got no business.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:28.915
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:28.915 --> 00:13:30.217
I hope you enjoyed the video.

00:13:30.217 --> 00:13:32.935
I made it because Iain
Fairley asked me to.

00:13:32.935 --> 00:13:34.428
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:13:34.428 --> 00:13:36.024
that you want me to profile next,

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:38.494
leave it in the comments below,
and I'll see what I can do.

00:13:38.494 --> 00:13:39.769
I'd also love to know

00:13:39.769 --> 00:13:42.845
which of Alan Sugar's top 10
rules meant the most to you.

00:13:42.845 --> 00:13:44.913
Leave it in the comments,
I'll join in the discussion.

00:13:44.913 --> 00:13:47.540
Thank you so much for
watching, continue to believe,

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.051
and I'll see you soon.

00:13:49.051 --> 00:13:50.091
(whooshing)

00:13:50.091 --> 00:13:52.258
(booming)

00:13:54.839 --> 00:13:57.747
- [Man] Do you think
source like Apprentice

00:13:57.747 --> 00:14:01.914
have genuinely a positive
impact on entrepreneurship?

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.121
- You mean, the program?

00:14:04.121 --> 00:14:04.954
- [Man] Yeah.

00:14:04.954 --> 00:14:05.787
- Okay, okay.

00:14:05.787 --> 00:14:09.290
- [Man] Because your program
is immensely successful.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:10.123
I love it.

00:14:10.123 --> 00:14:11.732
(audience laughing)

00:14:11.732 --> 00:14:15.270
We all watch it, but we
haven't seen big success--

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.752
- Okay, I think I get what
you're saying, but look.

00:14:17.752 --> 00:14:21.321
(audience laughing)

00:14:21.321 --> 00:14:24.128
I feel like I'm in the
boardroom, a candor bit there.

00:14:24.128 --> 00:14:28.045
No no, I think I know
where you're coming from.

00:14:28.895 --> 00:14:33.053
The thing is, is that you
might, you like the program.

00:14:33.053 --> 00:14:35.041
And I guess that you like it because

00:14:35.041 --> 00:14:38.177
you think it's entertaining and
you like looking at somebody

00:14:38.177 --> 00:14:40.742
you might think is a right numpty,

00:14:40.742 --> 00:14:43.593
and that's why you like it.

00:14:43.593 --> 00:14:46.741
What you don't realize in
the back of your mind is,

00:14:46.741 --> 00:14:49.751
is that you are picking up
some of the business message

00:14:49.751 --> 00:14:51.380
that is there, okay?

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.965
Now there was, well, you might
not admit it, but you are.

00:14:54.965 --> 00:14:56.882
And I can tell you that

00:14:59.594 --> 00:15:03.188
from when I started doing
this Apprentice thing,

00:15:03.188 --> 00:15:07.355
the amount of young people that
are inspired by the program,

00:15:08.242 --> 00:15:11.107
put aside all the fun and the laughter

00:15:11.107 --> 00:15:14.276
and all the clowns that you
think you've come across.

00:15:14.276 --> 00:15:16.547
The amount of people
that are inspired by it,

00:15:16.547 --> 00:15:19.130
the amount of people that were,

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:23.117
they put to me their business ideas.

00:15:23.117 --> 00:15:26.292
And I think it does, it performs a very,

00:15:26.292 --> 00:15:29.615
very good service amongst the
young, to be honest with you.

00:15:29.615 --> 00:15:33.717
And you can't get a
better endorsement of it

00:15:33.717 --> 00:15:36.006
when it becomes part of the curriculum

00:15:36.006 --> 00:15:39.324
at some schools where they set up a mini,

00:15:39.324 --> 00:15:42.199
a mini kind of apprentice task.

00:15:42.199 --> 00:15:44.919
And the amount of times
that I've been asked

00:15:44.919 --> 00:15:47.404
to attend schools to try and judge this.

00:15:47.404 --> 00:15:50.160
I just couldn't do them,
there's enough time in the day.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.107
So yes, it does inspire people.

00:15:52.107 --> 00:15:54.375
It entertains, and it inspires.

00:15:54.375 --> 00:15:56.708
- Who inspires you, and why?

00:15:58.003 --> 00:15:59.503
- Well, I don't...

00:16:01.089 --> 00:16:03.232
I wouldn't say that where I've got today

00:16:03.232 --> 00:16:07.149
is because I was inspired
by others, I think...

00:16:08.313 --> 00:16:11.106
The thing is, I often say to people that,

00:16:11.106 --> 00:16:13.689
you know, you're born
with a certain thing here.

00:16:13.689 --> 00:16:17.251
You know, this kind of gut feeling,

00:16:17.251 --> 00:16:20.159
this kind of determination,
you're born with it.

00:16:20.159 --> 00:16:22.924
I try to make the analogy of that,

00:16:22.924 --> 00:16:26.614
some people are born with a talent.

00:16:26.614 --> 00:16:29.293
If you locked me a room
with a piano teacher,

00:16:29.293 --> 00:16:31.978
for example, for one year,

00:16:31.978 --> 00:16:34.449
no doubt at the end, I
could perhaps knock out

00:16:34.449 --> 00:16:37.924
a rendition of Roll Out the Barrel, maybe.

00:16:37.924 --> 00:16:40.684
Would I ever be a concert pianist?

00:16:40.684 --> 00:16:42.336
Not in a million years.

00:16:42.336 --> 00:16:46.174
Because in that example,
that person has a talent.

00:16:46.174 --> 00:16:49.106
And I think I was blessed
with some kind of talent

00:16:49.106 --> 00:16:53.663
of some kind, you see,
which, an eye for things,

00:16:53.663 --> 00:16:57.754
a very fast brain to
see the end conclusion.

00:16:57.754 --> 00:17:01.531
Normally, the end conclusion,
I'm very skeptical

00:17:01.531 --> 00:17:04.390
of what can go wrong,
and that is something,

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:07.687
I'm afraid to say, you can't
go and buy in a book somewhere

00:17:07.687 --> 00:17:11.571
or go and buy a bottle of
entrepreneur juice and boots,

00:17:11.571 --> 00:17:12.795
or something like that.

00:17:12.795 --> 00:17:15.432
You're either born with it or not.

00:17:15.432 --> 00:17:18.650
And it doesn't come out initially.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:22.413
It is normally others
that observe your aptitude

00:17:22.413 --> 00:17:24.545
and it is others that encourage you along.

00:17:24.545 --> 00:17:25.821
So in my career,

00:17:25.821 --> 00:17:28.329
I kind of always had
people that I respected

00:17:28.329 --> 00:17:30.329
and where was my first respect?

00:17:30.329 --> 00:17:32.500
Well, in my humble family,

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.530
it was to look up to an uncle of mine

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.738
who was the only one that had a business.

00:17:36.738 --> 00:17:39.287
He had a small shop not
far from here, actually,

00:17:39.287 --> 00:17:43.144
in Victoria, so he was
someone I looked up to.

00:17:43.144 --> 00:17:45.893
And of course, it didn't take very long

00:17:45.893 --> 00:17:49.648
that I passed him over,
and when I passed him over,

00:17:49.648 --> 00:17:51.403
the next person I looked up to

00:17:51.403 --> 00:17:54.535
was one of the guys that
I was buying stuff from.

00:17:54.535 --> 00:17:57.180
Because he was the man, you know?

00:17:57.180 --> 00:18:00.685
And then I passed him over, also.

00:18:00.685 --> 00:18:03.663
And eventually got up the
ladder 'til you reach someone

00:18:03.663 --> 00:18:06.472
by the name of Rupert
Murdoch, for example.

00:18:06.472 --> 00:18:08.817
I haven't passed him over, yet, but.

00:18:08.817 --> 00:18:12.228
And I never will, but
I mean, on that climb,

00:18:12.228 --> 00:18:14.810
there were great names
like Lord Weinstock,

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.489
for example, from GEC.

00:18:16.489 --> 00:18:20.458
Great people that I
admire for their skills

00:18:20.458 --> 00:18:21.723
and all that stuff.

00:18:21.723 --> 00:18:24.829
And that's the people you look up to.

00:18:24.829 --> 00:18:26.682
That's the motivation that you get.

00:18:26.682 --> 00:18:29.236
They have got there, and
they've done it somehow.

00:18:29.236 --> 00:18:31.319
So I'm going to do the same.

